cff-version: 1.2.0
title: arrayprobe
message: >-
  This is a port, not new science. If you use it, cite the ORIGINAL alongside this
  package, as the source of the methodology (see the references below) -- UIOOPS for anything computed by
  arrayprobe or arrayprobe_uiops, and SODA-2 for anything computed by
  arrayprobe_soda2. arrayprobe 0.1.0 is archived at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23574623, and is cited
  alongside either original, never in place of it. Much of the porting, testing and
  documentation was written with the help of Anthropic's Claude, under
  the author's direction; the author reviewed and is responsible for the
  result.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23574623
date-released: '2026-11-02'
authors:
  - family-names: Gupta
    given-names: Siddhant
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0663-4595"
# Sole author. CFF 1.2.0 has no
# contributors field, so the others are credited in README.md:
#   Advisors and collaborators: Joe O'Brien and Bobby Jackson (ANL), Greg
#   McFarquhar and Yongjie Huang (University of Oklahoma), Aaron Bansemer
#   (NCAR MMM).
#   Data providers: Peter Brechner and Saurabh Patil (University of Oklahoma).
repository-code: "https://github.com/sgupta92/arrayprobe"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23574623
    description: arrayprobe 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  Python translations of two optical-array-probe processing chains that turn raw airborne probe
  imagery into particle size distributions with no licensed software: UIOOPS v3.5
  (University of Illinois/Oklahoma), the default engine, validated against GNU Octave runs
  of its own sources, and NCAR's SODA-2, validated against GDL runs of its sources. An
  earlier translation of UIOOPS v3.1.4, not part of this package, reproduced archived
  products cell by cell. Opt-in enhancements carry corrections beyond the original codes.
keywords:
  - optical array probe
  - cloud microphysics
  - particle size distribution
  - 2D-S
  - HVPS
  - airborne in-situ
  - UIOOPS
  - SODA-2
license: BSD-3-Clause
references:
  - type: software
    title: "University of Illinois/Oklahoma Optical Array Probe (OAP) Processing Software"
    version: "v3.1.4"
    year: 2018
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.1285969"
    notes: >-
      The original. Cite this for the methodology; arrayprobe ports it, under the
      3-clause BSD licence, with the UIOOPS maintainers' permission. An earlier translation of
      v3.1.4, not part of this package, reproduced archived products, defects
      included. The default engine is a
      port of UIOOPS v3.5, in which the UIOOPS developers had already fixed several
      defects; those fixes are theirs. This package's own corrections for
      data-destroying defects (the 2D-S bin table and stray-pixel removal) are on
      by default in the v3.5 engine, each recorded in the run's .call stamp and
      each with an off switch (--protective off, --stray-pixel off); every other
      correction is opt-in.
    repository-code: "https://github.com/joefinlon/UIOPS"
    url: "https://zenodo.org/records/1285969"
    authors:
      - family-names: McFarquhar
        given-names: Greg M.
      - family-names: Finlon
        given-names: Joseph A.
      - family-names: Stechman
        given-names: Daniel M.
      - family-names: Wu
        given-names: Wei
      - family-names: Jackson
        given-names: Robert C.
      - family-names: Freer
        given-names: Matt
  - type: software
    title: "joefinlon/UIOPS: New Ellipse/Rectangle Fit Executables + Modified Holroyd Improvements"
    version: "v3.5"
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.18945998"
    notes: >-
      The UIOOPS release the default engine (arrayprobe_uiops) ports. Cite it beside
      the entry above for anything the v3.5 engine computes.
    repository-code: "https://github.com/joefinlon/UIOPS"
